import ExprTypes.Typing

/-!
# The hand module of EXPR's type soundness

HAND-WRITTEN, and empty: EXPR has no cell besides `<k>`, so nothing is typed by hand, and no rule
reads or writes such a cell. Everything is generated by `k2lean soundness`
(`k2lean/docs/design.md`, §3.3) from kimp's `expr.k` and the type checker `k/expr-typing.k`:
`Typing.lean` before this module, preservation in `Typed.lean` after it, and `soundness` in
`Soundness.lean`, from EXPR's `gen --progress` under the typing (`Progress.lean`).
-/
